# Search plan: ${vault_tag}

**Anchor, established first.** ${coverage_question} Record the answer with its sources (and every
conflicting figure for area, sub-basins or districts, side by side) before any theme search. Every
search below is bounded to the places on that list.

**Execution.** Eight search agents (themes T1 to T8) each run the listed lenses plus their own
variants and return scored candidate URLs to `temp/candidates-T<n>.md`. Four local-ingest agents
(L1 to L4) register the project's own evidence under `temp/local-ingest-protocol.md`. Search in
${languages}, local language first. Local terms: ${local_terms}.

| Theme (tenure types in view) | Lens A: breadth | Lens B: depth or canonical | Lens C: adversarial | Lens D: period-pinned |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| T1 Coverage, institutions, infrastructure (agency-control; anchor) | the authority's territory, districts, sub-basins, schemes, dams | the instruments that define the territory and the schemes under each level of government | overlapping or disputed authority | the current organisation and allocation instruments (${as_of}) |
| T2 Permits, licences, groundwater (modern-permit, regulatory-licence, exempt-declared-commercial) | water-use permits and approvals, groundwater permits, bottled-water and industrial abstraction | studies of permitting and groundwater governance in the area; exemptions for basic needs and smallholder farming | unpermitted abstraction, hotels or industry and groundwater, protests | the current permit rules |
| T3 Irrigation (agency-control, commonhold, informal) | named schemes, weirs, canals; water user associations and federations | local irrigation institutions and offices, rotation and planting calendars | user groups only on paper, water taking out of turn, upstream-downstream conflict | the current season's planting and allocation plan |
| T4 Drinking water (water-supply-contract, assumed, impossible, de-minimis) | utilities' intakes and springs, regional systems, community and village systems | studies of community water supply in the area | disputes between villages and utilities over springs; systems without permits | raw-water allocation in the current plan |
| T5 Custom, religion, culture (customary, religious-law, reserve-minimum-flow) | sacred springs and wells, water rituals, customary custodians, mosque, temple or church water | ethnographies of water ritual and custom in the area | contested customary claims; commodification of sacred sources | instruments recognising customary land or water |
| T6 Livelihoods water law does not address (unrecognised, informal) | sand and gravel extraction, river and reservoir fisheries, fish ponds, cage culture, river tourism, coastal farming, herding | livelihood studies | conflicts over extraction, fisheries or tourism | none |
| T7 Investment, hydropower, industry, large projects (investment-contract) | hydropower plants, industrial and energy users, estates, airports and new towns | concession and partnership agreements | land-and-water conflicts around large projects | none |
| T8 Literature and framework (all types; patterns) | water rights, legal pluralism, groundwater, land-water links, gender and water in the area | FAO water tenure publications; ${framework_sources} | critiques of the tenure framing and of state-centred water law | constitutional or court decisions on water law, if any |

At least one adversarial search per theme.

## Local-ingest lanes

- L1 Plans, allocations, registers: allocation plans, basin plans, permit registers, statistics.
- L2 Team analytic reports: flag any AI-drafted material as such.
- L3 Workshops, meetings, interviews: first-hand statements.
- L4 Project notes and published papers on the area (follow wiki digests to their originals).
